From 23c870d487a2978b63c65839df208b94d2ad5fa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dev <dev@example.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 08:30:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] B1: capability-layer skill entries (eo/capability_entries.py)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New backend/eo/capability_entries.py: a second store, separate from
  eo/skill_library.py's semantic-retrieval skill docs (registry:
  capability_entries, exact tag lookup, no Vector/embedding step).
  entry_type is generic ("capability" here; Patch B2 reuses this same
  store/write path for "redaction" entries).
- CAPABILITY_SEED: three real starting entries — frontend_renderable_tabs,
  agent_roster, mcp_capabilities — sourced from frontend/app/components/
  tabs/*.jsx, eo/registry.py's ROLE_PROMPTS_SEED, and
  backend/config/mcp_servers.json.
- backend/eo/capabilities.py: new list_capabilities(tags=None), the
  tagged capability lookup eo agents and later patches (B3, B5b) call
  before falling back to introspection (B4). Only ever returns
  entry_type="capability" entries — redaction entries are a separate,
  non-default lookup, not reachable through this function.
- Tests: backend/tests/unit/test_eo_capability_entries.py (seed
  bootstrap, tag filtering, write-updates-in-place, entry_type
  discrimination incl. the B2 redaction case) and an extension to
  test_eo_capabilities.py pinning list_capabilities()'s delegation.
- Logic additionally hand-verified end-to-end against a stub
  memory.bus (fastapi/pydantic unavailable in this sandbox to run the
  real test suite) — see PR notes.

Ref: MiniMe-CLI-Internal-Architecture-Plan.md §3.2 (capability layer half)
Ref: MiniMe-Patch-Series-B-Plan.md, Patch B1
Depends on: Patch B0 (eo/capabilities.py must exist)
